The attached image illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, a dendrimer-like α-D-glucan. Panel (A) is a transmission electron microscopy (TEM) image, showing the spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like appearance, consistent with previous findings. The size bar indicates 50 nm, confirming their nanoscale. Panel (B) presents the diameter distribution of Nano-11 determined by dynamic light scattering (DLS), revealing a fairly uniform size distribution with a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter ranging from 75 to 80 nm. These characteristics are crucial for their efficient uptake by dendritic cells and their immunostimulatory properties as a vaccine adjuvant.